+# Trailer brief: <Game title> — <type> (<slug>)
+
+Fill this with the user before any capture. Every field gets an answer or "n/a"; the user approves the brief
+(chain phase "Brief" asks). Fields after Derek Lieu's creative brief; see references/craft.md.
+
+## Decisions
+- **Type:** gameplay | announce | launch | festival | tell-show-repeat | social  (Steam slot 1 = gameplay)
+- **Core message (one sentence):**
+- **Target length:** __ s (type range in references/beat-sheets.md)
+- **Platforms / exports:** Steam master 1080p, YouTube, vertical 9:16 (Shorts/TikTok); X optional
+- **CTA:** Wishlist on Steam | Play the demo now | Out now | ...  — **date / window:**
+- **Pass score for the trailer review:** 7 (frozen now; reviewers' minimum score must reach it)
+
+## The game
+- **Game description (2-3 lines):**
+- **Genre (and what a fan expects to see in the first 2 shots):**
+- **Hook (the one thing no other game in the genre does) and the shot that shows it:**
+- **2-3 pillars:** 1. … 2. … 3. …
+- **Player fantasy ("show the dream, not the job"):**
+- **Target audience ("fans of X and Y"):**
+
+## Tone and look
+- **Vibe / mood / tone (three words, ideally TASTE.md's):**
+- **Visual direction (palette, camera, pixel art: yes/no → scale_filter neighbor):**
+- **Music direction (genre, tempo, energy curve; ElevenLabs composition plan or licensed track):**
+- **VO: none | narrator | character lines** — voice and language:
+- **Reference trailers (links + what to borrow):**
+
+## Constraints
+- **Don'ts and spoilers (bosses, endings, unfinished areas, debug UI):**
+- **Rating bug / legal lines required:**
+- **Fonts and logo assets (TMP font asset path, logo PNG path):**
+- **Audio middleware:** Unity built-in audio | FMOD | Wwise (FMOD/Wwise are not captured by the Recorder:
+  record game audio separately or rebuild it in the edit)
+- **Deadline / timeline:**
+- **AI-generated content allowed:** music | VO | SFX (never footage). Recorded in REPORT.md for the Steam content survey.
+
+## Campaign
+- **Where it lives (Steam slot 1/2, YouTube, festival page, social):**
+- **Campaign goal (wishlists, demo plays, press):**
